<title>DENMARK: HEATWAVE RAISES DENMARK GRAIN HARVEST PROSPECTS.</title>
<headline>HEATWAVE RAISES DENMARK GRAIN HARVEST PROSPECTS.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark seems headed for an excellent grain harvest this year, aided by a wave of hot weather, the Danish Agricultural Advisory Centre said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still far too early to predict whether we will have a record harvest this year or not, but I do not think it is going to be a bad harvest at all,&quot; a spokesman for the centre told Ritzau, the Danish national news agency.</p>
<p>Grain harvesting is in progress throughout the country.</p>
<p>&quot;Winter barley has been harvested now and it is dry...It looks like there will be more rape this year than normally, while spring barley does not look like reaching recent years' levels,&quot; a spokesman for DLG, one of the country's leading grain producers, said.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
